-- title:
--   Levelwise maps from a formal quotient datum to X
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$, a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ that is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible $\pi\in\mathcal O$ with $\mathcal O$ complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, residue cardinality $\#(\mathcal O/\pi)=r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$, and a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ that is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$-algebra with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, such that every element of $Onr$ satisfies mod $\pi$ a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root mod $\pi$, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^r \pmod \pi$. Let $v\!\det:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ satisfy $v\!\det(g)=n$ iff $\det g=u\pi^n$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^\times$. Let $\sigma:G\to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ be a group homomorphism, $\Gamma,\Gamma'\le G$, with some $z\in\Gamma$ such that $\sigma z$ is scalar with $v\!\det(\sigma z)=2$, and some $w\in\Gamma$ with $v\!\det(\sigma w)=1$. Let $f:\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ be a scheme over $\mathcal O$, and let $\Theta$ assign, to every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map from pairs $(\psi,P)$ with $\psi:Onr\to_{\mathcal O} B$ an algebra map and $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$ (an object of `Omega K₀ π` at $B$) to morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}B\to\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$; assume $\Theta$ is natural in $B$, invariant under the twisted action of $\Gamma$ (`OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct`: $\psi'$ is the $-v\!\det(\sigma\gamma)$-fold Frobenius twist of $\psi$ and $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$), and, for every algebraically closed field $k$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and every fixed $\psi:Onr\to_{\mathcal O}k$, that $P\mapsto\Theta_k(\psi,P)$ is surjective onto the $k$-points of $f$ with fibres exactly the twisted $\Gamma$-orbits. Let $g_1\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and let $D$ be a formal quotient datum for these data, with proper structure morphisms $y\!b_n:D.Y_n\to\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$, transitions $y\!t_n:D.Y_n\to D.Y_{n+1}$ and universal families $q_n$. Let $sR_n$ be $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathcal O\to\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$, let $tR_n$ be morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})\to\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+2})$ with $tR_n$ followed by $sR_{n+1}$ equal to $sR_n$, and let $x_n:\mathcal X_n\to\mathcal X_{n+1}$ be morphisms between the pullbacks $\mathcal X_n:=\mathcal X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O}\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ commuting with the first projections and with the second projections through $tR_n$. Then there are morphisms $v_n:D.Y_n\to\mathcal X_n$ such that: $v_n$ followed by the second projection is $y\!b_n$; for each $n$ the square with top $y\!t_n$, left $v_n$, right $v_{n+1}$ and bottom $x_n$ is cartesian; for every $n$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi^{n+1}=0$ in $B$ and every pair $x=(\psi,P)$ over $B$, the composite $q_n(x)$, $v_n$, first projection equals the morphism underlying $\Theta_B(x)$; and for every algebraically closed field $K$, composition with $v_n$ is injective on morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}K\to D.Y_n$.
--
--   This is the levelwise comparison step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: the truncations $D.Y_n$ of the formal quotient attached to the $p$-adic upper half plane and the group $\Gamma$ are matched, compatibly with the transition maps and with the uniformisation map $\Theta$, against the truncations $\mathcal X\times_{\mathcal O}\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$ of the target curve, with $v_n$ injective on geometric points. It feeds the algebraisation of the resulting system and is used in the identification of the Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient, in the construction of charts on it, and in the description of its adic points.
